          },
          {
            "heading": "How he thinks about the tool",
            "content": "Taylor describes AI as a personalized tutor that can teach in the way a child learns best—visually, through audio, or through reading—and can test or quiz them. He encourages children to make AI part of their lives and views it more like Google Search or a utility for learning than like a mobile phone, which he says he would wait a long time to give a child. He also cautions that the technology can help students avoid learning, so parents and teachers face a challenge.",
            "citation_ids": [
              "S1",
